  "problem": "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+\\frac{4}{x}y=-6{x}^{2}{y}^{3/2},\\,y(1)=\\frac{1}{9},\\,y>0.\n$$\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the fact that the given differential equation can be transformed into the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{2}{x}\\,z=3{x}^{2}\n$$\n\nusing the substitution $z={y}^{-1/2}.$*",
